\ Dogfood: Phase 4 slice 6h. The raw array constructor `[ Type ; Count ]`
\ allocs one array slot and zero-inits its contents with a counted loop. Every
\ probe runs *after* `dirty`, which fills a same-or-larger array with a nonzero
\ seed and returns, so the constructor reuses a stack region full of 99s: a
\ zero read then proves the zero-init loop ran, not that fresh stack happened
\ to be zero. Without the preamble these are placebos (`Alloc` never zeroes).

: dirty ( -- ) 99 10 fill drop ;

\ `[ i64 ; 10 ]`: index 9 reads 0 after the dirty preamble.
: probe10 ( -- i64 )
  [ i64 ; 10 ] | a | &a 9 >usize &> @ | v | a drop v ;

\ `[ i8 ; 10 ]` (size 10 / align 1): index 9 reads 0 and a live neighbour
\ (`guard`, a `[i64 3]` of 5s) stays intact, so a word-granular overrun of the
\ unpadded array would show up as a clobbered neighbour.
: probe_i8 ( -- i8 i64 )
  5 3 fill | guard |
  [ i8 ; 10 ] | a | &a 9 >usize &> @ | v | a drop
  &guard 0 >usize &> @ | g | guard drop
  v g ;

\ `[ bool ; 4 ]`: every slot is variant 0 (`false`), not a garbage byte (which
\ prints `true`), so a `false`x4 output can only come from the zero-init.
: probe_bool ( -- )
  [ bool ; 4 ] | a |
  &a 0 >usize &> @ .
  &a 1 >usize &> @ .
  &a 2 >usize &> @ .
  &a 3 >usize &> @ .
  a drop ;

\ Terms after the constructor's own loop are not dropped (the `terminated`
\ reset), and a `times` after it composes (loop-state hygiene).
: probe_after ( -- )
  [ i64 ; 4 ] | a | a drop
  100 .
  3 [ | i | i . ] times
  200 . ;

\ D5: a concrete `[ i64 ; 4 ]` inside a combinator body works for free.
: withbuf ( [ -- i64 ] -- i64 )
  | f | [ i64 ; 4 ] | a | &a 0 >usize &> @ | z | a drop f call z + ;

\ A self-tail-recursive word that constructs an array each iteration: the
\ constructor's loop opens *inside* the word's own self-tail loop, so without
\ the save/restore loop-state hygiene the enclosing loop's back-edge is sealed
\ against the wrong header (a compiler panic). `z` is the zero-init index 0.
: recur ( i64 -- )
  | n | [ i64 ; 4 ] | a | &a 0 >usize &> @ | z | a drop
  n z + .
  n 0 > if n 1 - recur else end ;

: main ( -- )
  dirty probe10 .        \ 0
  dirty probe_i8 . .     \ 5 0
  dirty probe_bool       \ false false false false
  dirty probe_after      \ 100 0 1 2 200
  [ 5 ] withbuf .        \ 5
  dirty 3 recur ;        \ 3 2 1 0
